# Video Asset URLs

MediaConvert Lambda generates these outputs for every uploaded video:

| Output | Suffix |
|--------|--------|
| 1080p video | `-1080p.mp4` |
| 720p video | `-720p.mp4` |
| Original | `-original.mp4` |
| Thumbnail | `-thumb.0000000.jpg` |

To derive a thumbnail URL, replace the quality suffix: `{base}-1080p.mp4` → `{base}-thumb.0000000.jpg`.
NEVER guess patterns like `-poster.jpg` or `-thumbnail.jpg`.

CDN base URLs:

- Preferred: `https://media.vibrationfit.com/site-assets/video/...`
- S3 direct: `https://vibration-fit-client-storage.s3.amazonaws.com/site-assets/video/...`

## Video component

The `<Video>` component from `@/lib/design-system/components` auto-derives the thumbnail from `src` when no `poster` prop is given — do not manually specify posters for MediaConvert-processed videos. Use `getVideoThumbnailUrl(videoUrl)` (same import) outside the component.
